1
00:00:00,695 --> 00:00:03,435
(I'm Back)

2
00:00:05,205 --> 00:00:07,235
Gosh, I haven't driven on this road in a while.

3
00:00:09,135 --> 00:00:12,775
(She drives past a serene, green field...)

4
00:00:14,345 --> 00:00:18,685
(and quietly heads somewhere.)

5
00:00:36,665 --> 00:00:38,805
(Na Rae leans on her car and wipes away her tears.)

6
00:00:40,735 --> 00:00:43,435
(Soon after, she starts walking with heaviness in her steps.)

7
00:00:50,545 --> 00:00:54,245
(She crouches down after barely taking a few steps.)

8
00:01:07,125 --> 00:01:10,895
(She musters up her courage and stands in front of the gate.)

9
00:01:13,405 --> 00:01:14,705
This is so hard. What am I going to do?

10
00:01:26,685 --> 00:01:28,885
Grandma, Grandpa. I'm here.

11
00:01:32,985 --> 00:01:34,085
Oh, no.

12
00:01:41,065 --> 00:01:43,795
(With no friendly greetings returned,)

13
00:01:46,065 --> 00:01:49,505
(the house is filled with only silence.)

14
00:01:57,675 --> 00:02:00,914
(It's the house of her grandparents...)

15
00:02:00,915 --> 00:02:02,884
- Grandma! - My gosh.

16
00:02:02,885 --> 00:02:08,625
(she loved with all of her heart.)

17
00:02:09,055 --> 00:02:10,225
Come on in.

18
00:02:10,395 --> 00:02:11,925
- Grandma! - Hey.

19
00:02:12,425 --> 00:02:17,694
(Her family used to give her a warm welcome from the gate.)

20
00:02:17,695 --> 00:02:18,904
Did you drive here?

21
00:02:18,905 --> 00:02:19,935
Yes.

22
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:21,275
All right.

23
00:02:21,935 --> 00:02:28,814
(She made unforgettable memories with her grandparents at the house.)

24
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:31,045
I like it. It's beautiful.

25
00:02:31,215 --> 00:02:32,645
I'm so proud of you, Na Rae.

26
00:02:34,685 --> 00:02:38,555
(Grandma, Grandpa. I'm here.)

27
00:02:51,405 --> 00:02:52,505
How am I going to do this?

28
00:02:54,605 --> 00:02:55,674
(She's unable to move at the unfamiliar sight.)

29
00:02:55,675 --> 00:02:57,474
Their house was always clean.

30
00:02:57,475 --> 00:02:59,604
I just couldn't believe my eyes when I saw how messy it was.

31
00:02:59,605 --> 00:03:00,805
I don't think I could've gone inside.

32
00:03:01,345 --> 00:03:03,714
It was your 1st time seeing the house after 2 years, right?

33
00:03:03,715 --> 00:03:04,744
- Yes. - Right.

34
00:03:04,745 --> 00:03:06,384
- I only saw it from a distance. - I see.

35
00:03:06,385 --> 00:03:08,085
- Going in must've terrified you. - Right.

36
00:03:14,725 --> 00:03:19,525
(She braces herself and enters the house.)

37
00:03:29,775 --> 00:03:31,204
Everything looks the same.

38
00:03:31,205 --> 00:03:35,245
(The pictures are hanging in the same spots as before.)

39
00:03:47,655 --> 00:03:49,525
Oh, no.

40
00:03:53,565 --> 00:03:55,135
The pictures are still hanging here.

41
00:04:00,305 --> 00:04:02,075
The massage chair I bought for them is still here.

42
00:04:07,275 --> 00:04:08,545
After my grandparents passed away...

43
00:04:09,445 --> 00:04:11,884
You know, there's a healthy period for grieving.

44
00:04:11,885 --> 00:04:13,445
But I couldn't give myself time to grieve.

45
00:04:14,785 --> 00:04:16,685
I had this dream every day.

46
00:04:16,885 --> 00:04:19,555
In my dream, my grandma looked so healthy.

47
00:04:20,085 --> 00:04:22,954
When I woke up from it, I believed it to be real.

48
00:04:22,955 --> 00:04:23,995
Then ten minutes later,

49
00:04:24,555 --> 00:04:26,224
I'd realise that she had passed away.

50
00:04:26,225 --> 00:04:28,064
And all of a sudden, I'd cry at night.

51
00:04:28,065 --> 00:04:31,094
I thought I would break down if I went back to their house.

52
00:04:31,095 --> 00:04:33,264
So I've been putting it off.

53
00:04:33,265 --> 00:04:35,434
(So I couldn't come here.)

54
00:04:35,435 --> 00:04:38,804
Actually, six months before my grandpa's passing,

55
00:04:38,805 --> 00:04:41,045
my grandparents moved into a nursing hospital together.

56
00:04:41,345 --> 00:04:43,274
My grandpa passed away all of a sudden.

57
00:04:43,275 --> 00:04:45,484
Then my grandma stayed at the nursing hospital.

58
00:04:45,485 --> 00:04:48,515
Our family took turns to look after them.

59
00:04:48,985 --> 00:04:52,855
No one had the time or energy to fix up the house or do anything.

60
00:04:53,625 --> 00:04:56,394
This house was the last thing on our mind.

61
00:04:56,395 --> 00:04:57,425
Then...

62
00:04:57,995 --> 00:05:02,035
my uncle came to the house and tried to clean it up.

63
00:05:02,595 --> 00:05:05,335
It must've been too much for him to handle alone.

64
00:05:05,935 --> 00:05:08,404
At her funeral, I told my family that I would take care of it.

65
00:05:08,405 --> 00:05:09,905
(I decided to help with the rest of the house.)

66
00:05:10,175 --> 00:05:11,235
Actually,

67
00:05:12,875 --> 00:05:15,115
my family cleaned some parts of the house.

68
00:05:15,615 --> 00:05:19,384
There were a few last items they couldn't sort out.

69
00:05:19,385 --> 00:05:23,185
I told them I would take care of them.

70
00:05:23,715 --> 00:05:25,454
It took a lot of courage on my part...

71
00:05:25,455 --> 00:05:28,194
to visit their house after two years.

72
00:05:28,195 --> 00:05:29,255
I see.

73
00:05:29,455 --> 00:05:31,725
So, I...

74
00:05:35,995 --> 00:05:39,064
I couldn't calm down.

75
00:05:39,065 --> 00:05:40,435
(Overwhelmed by profound sadness, she struggled to calm down.)

76
00:05:41,235 --> 00:05:42,434
They were in my dream every day.

77
00:05:42,435 --> 00:05:44,375
But I just couldn't bring myself to go to their house.

78
00:05:45,805 --> 00:05:46,874
It's not easy.

79
00:05:46,875 --> 00:05:48,215
(Right, it's not easy.)

80
00:05:48,875 --> 00:05:50,345
This requires courage too.

81
00:05:51,815 --> 00:05:53,215
- It was too much for me to handle. - Yes.

82
00:06:02,625 --> 00:06:03,754
Hold on.

83
00:06:03,755 --> 00:06:06,794
(With courage, she studies the traces of her grandparents.)

84
00:06:06,795 --> 00:06:07,825
Hold on.

85
00:06:10,295 --> 00:06:12,134
(Her grandma used to cool the water in case it was too hot...)

86
00:06:12,135 --> 00:06:14,005
(for her grown-up granddaughter.)

87
00:06:15,335 --> 00:06:17,105
(At her grandma's usual spot...)

88
00:06:17,435 --> 00:06:19,004
(Before breakfast, after breakfast, after lunch, after dinner)

89
00:06:19,005 --> 00:06:22,015
(Only a trace of frozen time lingers.)

90
00:06:26,185 --> 00:06:27,245
This is our house.

91
00:06:28,455 --> 00:06:31,785
I was born and lived here until I was nine years old.

92
00:06:32,155 --> 00:06:33,255
And...

93
00:06:35,095 --> 00:06:36,524
this is my grandparents' house.

94
00:06:36,525 --> 00:06:38,925
(The house of my dear grandparents)

95
00:06:39,995 --> 00:06:41,794
- Don't give me a lot of rice. - Why not?

96
00:06:41,795 --> 00:06:42,995
I'm on a diet.

97
00:06:43,965 --> 00:06:45,365
You're all skin and bones.

98
00:06:45,965 --> 00:06:47,604
(The house...)

99
00:06:47,605 --> 00:06:49,074
I hope you don't have to leave.

100
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:51,074
(where people who cherished and loved me once lived)

101
00:06:51,075 --> 00:06:56,215
(where people who cherished and loved me once lived)

102
00:07:15,135 --> 00:07:18,265
(She pulls weeds in the yard with her bare hands.)

103
00:07:22,275 --> 00:07:23,835
Watch your hands.

104
00:07:24,675 --> 00:07:26,405
That was the furthest thing from my mind.

105
00:07:30,075 --> 00:07:32,285
They're completely overgrown.

106
00:07:41,055 --> 00:07:43,925
Gosh, I can't seem to pull this out. This is so annoying.

107
00:07:51,805 --> 00:07:53,634
I noticed later that I had scraped my hands.

108
00:07:53,635 --> 00:07:56,035
Back then, I didn't feel any pain. I just couldn't stand still.

109
00:07:57,975 --> 00:07:59,645
It took too long for me to come back here.

110
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:06,385
(In no time, there's a pile of weeds in the yard.)

111
00:08:07,645 --> 00:08:09,485
The overgrown weeds...

112
00:08:11,015 --> 00:08:14,725
Seriously. They looked so awful.

113
00:08:15,195 --> 00:08:16,725
I wanted to pull all of them out.

114
00:08:23,195 --> 00:08:24,295
They're all broken.

115
00:08:27,265 --> 00:08:28,505
My grandma used to cherish them.

116
00:08:33,405 --> 00:08:34,875
They must've been outside for too long.

117
00:08:39,145 --> 00:08:40,245
This is the only one that's not broken.

118
00:08:43,515 --> 00:08:44,655
All done.

119
00:08:59,235 --> 00:09:00,305
Park Na Rae.

120
00:09:01,305 --> 00:09:02,435
Na Rae.

121
00:09:04,435 --> 00:09:05,505
Na Rae.

122
00:09:06,105 --> 00:09:07,375
Open the gate.

123
00:09:14,185 --> 00:09:17,255
My gosh. Look at you. You've been crying.

124
00:09:20,625 --> 00:09:22,824
- It was a long trip, right? - Why are you crying?

125
00:09:22,825 --> 00:09:23,895
When did you get here?

126
00:09:24,395 --> 00:09:25,495
An hour ago.

127
00:09:28,065 --> 00:09:30,935
(Patting her on the back without saying a word)

128
00:09:33,465 --> 00:09:35,805
I once talked to Kian84 and Hyun Moo about this.

129
00:09:36,035 --> 00:09:39,605
I told them that I wanted to be the one...

130
00:09:40,175 --> 00:09:42,175
to take down their pictures.

131
00:09:42,545 --> 00:09:43,815
I told them that...

132
00:09:44,175 --> 00:09:47,145
I wanted this house to always be clean and cosy...

133
00:09:47,345 --> 00:09:51,154
just like when they were alive.

134
00:09:51,155 --> 00:09:53,155
You were so young. Gosh, look how young you were.

135
00:09:55,225 --> 00:09:58,664
Then they were willing to come and help me.

136
00:09:58,665 --> 00:10:01,365
So I'm so grateful that they came all this way.

137
00:10:02,195 --> 00:10:03,264
It's been eight years...

138
00:10:03,265 --> 00:10:04,965
since you visited her grandma's house, right?

139
00:10:05,365 --> 00:10:06,404
It's been eight years.

140
00:10:06,405 --> 00:10:07,635
- Really? - Yes.

141
00:10:08,005 --> 00:10:10,035
Seeing how she wanted both of us, there must be a lot of work.

142
00:10:10,235 --> 00:10:12,005
They came early in the morning.

143
00:10:12,505 --> 00:10:13,705
I wonder if the wooden bench is still there.

144
00:10:14,375 --> 00:10:15,474
- Do you remember it? - Yes.

145
00:10:15,475 --> 00:10:16,574
Na Rae gave us cold coffee there.

146
00:10:16,575 --> 00:10:17,915
Yes, that's right.

147
00:10:18,015 --> 00:10:19,785
You know what I remember?

148
00:10:20,145 --> 00:10:21,545
We cooked ginseng chicken soup.

149
00:10:22,615 --> 00:10:24,515
It feels like that was 18 years ago, not 8 years.

150
00:10:25,185 --> 00:10:26,225
It's been so long.

151
00:10:26,625 --> 00:10:29,094
They came all this way just because I asked.

152
00:10:29,095 --> 00:10:31,495
This wasn't an easy thing to do. I was so grateful.

153
00:10:32,065 --> 00:10:35,335
As we told you before, we also have a lot of memories...

154
00:10:35,565 --> 00:10:37,194
- about the house. - Right.

155
00:10:37,195 --> 00:10:39,204
- We had a good memory there. - Right.

156
00:10:39,205 --> 00:10:41,804
- We had so much fun. - It felt like...

157
00:10:41,805 --> 00:10:43,774
being on summer vacation from school...

158
00:10:43,775 --> 00:10:45,674
- Right. - as grown-ups.

159
00:10:45,675 --> 00:10:47,875
- We had fun like school kids. - We did.

160
00:10:48,515 --> 00:10:52,085
She recalled our memory from eight years ago...

161
00:10:52,585 --> 00:10:55,615
and asked me to help her. I was grateful for that.

162
00:10:57,655 --> 00:11:01,025
Actually, my paternal grandmother passed away...

163
00:11:01,185 --> 00:11:02,654
when I was 20 years old.

164
00:11:02,655 --> 00:11:05,865
My maternal grandmother passed away before I turned 30.

165
00:11:06,365 --> 00:11:07,424
When I was young,

166
00:11:07,425 --> 00:11:09,465
I was going to follow my grandma once she passed.

167
00:11:09,635 --> 00:11:11,335
- I was like that as a kid. - Same here.

168
00:11:13,335 --> 00:11:14,565
Given my history,

169
00:11:15,705 --> 00:11:17,805
I could understand what she was going through.

170
00:11:18,745 --> 00:11:21,505
When I was about to enter the house, even I thought...

171
00:11:21,875 --> 00:11:24,374
I couldn't walk in. You know what I mean?

172
00:11:24,375 --> 00:11:25,545
This house means...

173
00:11:26,645 --> 00:11:30,215
This kind of emotion must have hit Na Rae harder than it hit me.

174
00:11:30,955 --> 00:11:32,755
I got emotional too.

175
00:11:33,085 --> 00:11:35,795
When she opened the gate, I saw her puffy eyes.

176
00:11:36,495 --> 00:11:39,325
I got emotional too. But I couldn't break down with her.

177
00:11:39,465 --> 00:11:41,525
I thought that would make her break down in tears.

178
00:11:41,695 --> 00:11:44,565
So I pretended to be indifferent about that.

179
00:11:44,835 --> 00:11:45,935
Sit down.

180
00:11:46,535 --> 00:11:49,875
- You made us cold coffee here. - Right, the bench is still here.

181
00:11:50,075 --> 00:11:51,075
It's still here.

182
00:11:51,435 --> 00:11:53,175
- But everything here is... - Yes?

183
00:11:53,345 --> 00:11:55,644
worn down and rusty.

184
00:11:55,645 --> 00:11:57,075
I might have to throw everything out.

185
00:11:59,715 --> 00:12:01,885
I couldn't handle it. I didn't know where to start.

186
00:12:02,615 --> 00:12:03,785
I bet you felt lost.

187
00:12:05,255 --> 00:12:06,654
We'll do whatever you want.

188
00:12:06,655 --> 00:12:08,354
This is...

189
00:12:08,355 --> 00:12:10,725
- I don't know where to start. - Right. This is...

190
00:12:10,895 --> 00:12:12,064
Let's throw out some things.

191
00:12:12,065 --> 00:12:13,565
Why don't we go over there?

192
00:12:13,725 --> 00:12:14,824
- Show us around. - Okay.

193
00:12:14,825 --> 00:12:16,594
- I had to show them inside. - Yes.

194
00:12:16,595 --> 00:12:18,705
I remember spending the night here.

195
00:12:19,205 --> 00:12:20,264
Right.

196
00:12:20,265 --> 00:12:22,904
They cleaned the floor, so it's clean inside.

197
00:12:22,905 --> 00:12:24,104
Let's take off our shoes.

198
00:12:24,105 --> 00:12:25,145
This is...

199
00:12:27,405 --> 00:12:28,645
It still smells the same.

200
00:12:28,875 --> 00:12:30,015
The smell of a house in the countryside.

201
00:12:30,275 --> 00:12:32,345
Yes. I remember the house.

202
00:12:32,885 --> 00:12:34,014
Look. That's us.

203
00:12:34,015 --> 00:12:36,014
(Look at the photo of us.)

204
00:12:36,015 --> 00:12:37,855
- My goodness. - Hey.

205
00:12:38,385 --> 00:12:40,185
- My goodness. - Hey. When was that?

206
00:12:40,955 --> 00:12:43,594
My grandparents really loved you guys.

207
00:12:43,595 --> 00:12:45,294
- My grandparents loved them. - Oh, my.

208
00:12:45,295 --> 00:12:46,824
I didn't know they hung the photo here.

209
00:12:46,825 --> 00:12:48,835
- They were so healthy back then. - Right.

210
00:12:49,635 --> 00:12:52,365
- So I couldn't bring myself... - How sad.

211
00:12:52,605 --> 00:12:54,065
to take down these pictures.

212
00:12:54,505 --> 00:12:57,475
But why do you want to take them down?

213
00:12:58,435 --> 00:13:02,244
First of all, there's a leak in the house.

214
00:13:02,245 --> 00:13:03,814
The wallpapers are so mouldy.

215
00:13:03,815 --> 00:13:04,974
Once one part gets mouldy,

216
00:13:04,975 --> 00:13:06,985
- it will spread all over the house. - It will spread.

217
00:13:07,215 --> 00:13:08,814
So I learned how to put up wallpapers...

218
00:13:08,815 --> 00:13:11,255
and plaster the walls, so I could fix the ceiling.

219
00:13:11,585 --> 00:13:15,454
But I must take them down to fix up the house.

220
00:13:15,455 --> 00:13:17,154
But I just couldn't take...

221
00:13:17,155 --> 00:13:19,264
- the photos down myself. - That's understandable.

222
00:13:19,265 --> 00:13:21,825
- You want to do some repair work. - Yes.

223
00:13:21,995 --> 00:13:23,494
If we leave the house as it is,

224
00:13:23,495 --> 00:13:25,634
- it might be a deserted house. - The house will be ruined.

225
00:13:25,635 --> 00:13:27,935
- The house will be damaged. - Right.

226
00:13:28,735 --> 00:13:30,835
I don't know where to begin.

227
00:13:31,945 --> 00:13:33,375
We have to report the items before throwing them out, right?

228
00:13:33,575 --> 00:13:35,104
I think we passed that point.

229
00:13:35,105 --> 00:13:37,944
- Right. - We need to hire a service for it.

230
00:13:37,945 --> 00:13:40,845
I have so much stuff to throw out in the yard.

231
00:13:41,385 --> 00:13:42,484
I'm glad they went.

232
00:13:42,485 --> 00:13:43,984
- Kian84 is a hard worker. - Right.

233
00:13:43,985 --> 00:13:45,115
Hyun Moo too.

234
00:13:45,855 --> 00:13:47,585
- You included me out of respect. - Yes.

235
00:13:47,925 --> 00:13:49,994
You know what? Having them there was a huge help.

236
00:13:49,995 --> 00:13:51,255
- I mean it. - Right.

237
00:13:51,455 --> 00:13:53,724
You need someone to decide on the order.

238
00:13:53,725 --> 00:13:56,394
Someone who can make sound judgment and prioritise.

239
00:13:56,395 --> 00:13:58,135
- Hyun Moo was great at that. - Yes.

240
00:13:58,435 --> 00:13:59,834
Hyun Moo did things that required thinking.

241
00:13:59,835 --> 00:14:01,204
And I took care of physical tasks.

242
00:14:01,205 --> 00:14:02,535
- That's a nice way of putting it. - Yes.

243
00:14:02,805 --> 00:14:03,875
"Thinking."

244
00:14:04,235 --> 00:14:05,804
(Scanning the house while thinking)

245
00:14:05,805 --> 00:14:08,005
What about the fridge? Will you throw it out?

246
00:14:09,215 --> 00:14:11,514
I'm not sure. But my uncle...

247
00:14:11,515 --> 00:14:14,645
took out all the food in the fridge.

248
00:14:15,015 --> 00:14:17,284
- The fridge still works. - Food...

249
00:14:17,285 --> 00:14:18,485
Is there another fridge here?

250
00:14:19,725 --> 00:14:21,424
That's the primary fridge.

251
00:14:21,425 --> 00:14:22,695
- And this is... - Is it a kimchi fridge?

252
00:14:24,595 --> 00:14:25,995
Gosh, it's kimchi.

253
00:14:26,365 --> 00:14:28,635
Oh, no. Did your grandma make it?

254
00:14:35,535 --> 00:14:38,705
(Kimchi made by her grandparents is still in the fridge.)

255
00:14:40,505 --> 00:14:43,915
(She bursts into tears at the sight of their trace.)

256
00:14:47,185 --> 00:14:48,614
Their kimchi holds...

257
00:14:48,615 --> 00:14:50,185
- a lot of meaning for me. - Right.

258
00:14:50,915 --> 00:14:53,255
- It was still in the fridge. - It was.

259
00:14:54,085 --> 00:14:57,595
I can't control myself right now.

260
00:15:03,395 --> 00:15:05,735
- Both of us... - Come on.

