518
00:23:58,865 --> 00:24:00,504
- No? - Your grandma's place is nearby.

519
00:24:00,505 --> 00:24:02,435
- Right. - You're sweating. It must be hot.

520
00:24:02,735 --> 00:24:04,774
- Sit there. - Did her grandma come here often?

521
00:24:04,775 --> 00:24:06,574
- Did she? - She came here often.

522
00:24:06,575 --> 00:24:07,705
- Really? - Yes.

523
00:24:07,975 --> 00:24:10,614
I thought that she liked cooking.

524
00:24:10,615 --> 00:24:12,614
- Come on. - She cooked a feast only for me.

525
00:24:12,615 --> 00:24:13,615
Of course.

526
00:24:13,616 --> 00:24:15,344
She cooked so much food whenever I came over.

527
00:24:15,345 --> 00:24:17,455
- She didn't want to cook sometimes. - Of course.

528
00:24:17,855 --> 00:24:19,484
What brings you here?

529
00:24:19,485 --> 00:24:22,485
We couldn't clean up my grandma's house.

530
00:24:22,995 --> 00:24:24,495
We're here to clean it up.

531
00:24:24,755 --> 00:24:26,325
They're going to help me.

532
00:24:26,595 --> 00:24:28,295
(I see.)

533
00:24:28,525 --> 00:24:30,835
- What's on the menu? - What should we get?

534
00:24:31,265 --> 00:24:34,205
The yukhoe bibimbap is our signature dish.

535
00:24:34,305 --> 00:24:35,704
Then give us three of that.

536
00:24:35,705 --> 00:24:36,675
- Let's order some soup. - We should...

537
00:24:36,676 --> 00:24:38,474
- order soup. - How about kimchi jjigae?

538
00:24:38,475 --> 00:24:39,544
I'm craving intestine soup too.

539
00:24:39,545 --> 00:24:40,844
- The intestine soup? - Try that too.

540
00:24:40,845 --> 00:24:42,074
One serving of the intestine soup...

541
00:24:42,075 --> 00:24:43,474
- and one serving of kimchi jjigae. - One serving of kimchi jjigae.

542
00:24:43,475 --> 00:24:45,644
- Three yukhoe bibimbap, please. - Bibimbap.

543
00:24:45,645 --> 00:24:47,385
- Yes. - You want to order that much food?

544
00:24:47,545 --> 00:24:50,584
My gosh. This meal is like an appetizer.

545
00:24:50,585 --> 00:24:52,855
- This is considered a small meal. - Right.

546
00:24:53,025 --> 00:24:55,154
- We need to work today. - You must have a filling meal.

547
00:24:55,155 --> 00:24:56,295
- Yes. - Gosh.

548
00:24:56,425 --> 00:24:57,894
I'll give you three.

549
00:24:57,895 --> 00:24:59,124
- Okay. - This looks great.

550
00:24:59,125 --> 00:25:00,494
- Thank you. - Hold on. One intestine soup,

551
00:25:00,495 --> 00:25:01,995
one yukhoe bibimbap...

552
00:25:02,125 --> 00:25:04,064
- What was the last one? - Three yukhoe bibimbap.

553
00:25:04,065 --> 00:25:06,004
- I see. Three? - Three yukhoe bibimbap.

554
00:25:06,005 --> 00:25:07,034
- Three yukhoe bibimbap? - She's quite surprised.

555
00:25:07,035 --> 00:25:08,804
- Kimchi jjigae and the soup too. - Kimchi jjigae too.

556
00:25:08,805 --> 00:25:10,104
- Look how surprised she is. - Yes.

557
00:25:10,105 --> 00:25:12,075
- All that for the three of you? - Yes.

558
00:25:12,175 --> 00:25:14,304
- That's 5 servings. - She and I can eat 5 servings.

559
00:25:14,305 --> 00:25:15,345
- Right. - Yes.

560
00:25:16,215 --> 00:25:17,714
- We eat a lot. - The kimchi jjigae is good.

561
00:25:17,715 --> 00:25:18,715
- Yes. - Yes.

562
00:25:20,415 --> 00:25:21,585
What about your grandma's kimchi?

563
00:25:23,215 --> 00:25:24,615
(Sighing)

564
00:25:25,285 --> 00:25:27,425
Usually, people can't seem to eat it.

565
00:25:28,085 --> 00:25:29,085
Should we...

566
00:25:29,086 --> 00:25:30,095
(Inhaling deeply)

567
00:25:31,755 --> 00:25:33,094
What are you going to say now?

568
00:25:33,095 --> 00:25:34,995
- You're making me nervous. - Should I sell that online too?

569
00:25:35,495 --> 00:25:39,095
I thought that you wouldn't be able to eat it.

570
00:25:39,505 --> 00:25:41,034
Wouldn't it be better if we ate it for you?

571
00:25:41,035 --> 00:25:43,405
What is this? Gosh, I have a headache.

572
00:25:43,675 --> 00:25:45,904
Her grandma made it to be consumed.

573
00:25:45,905 --> 00:25:47,144
- Right. - We can't throw that out.

574
00:25:47,145 --> 00:25:48,774
- We understand your intention. - Right.

575
00:25:48,775 --> 00:25:51,144
Na Rae sent me a lot of kimchi, so I ate a lot of her kimchi.

576
00:25:51,145 --> 00:25:53,184
He also asked for my grandma's bone soup.

577
00:25:53,185 --> 00:25:55,445
He can have a meal with the kimchi and the bone soup.

578
00:25:55,845 --> 00:25:57,884
- That's perfect. Yes. - What an excellent pairing.

579
00:25:57,885 --> 00:25:59,214
The 12-year-old bone soup...

580
00:25:59,215 --> 00:26:00,784
- with the two-year-old kimchi. - Yes.

581
00:26:00,785 --> 00:26:02,555
- That's a total of 17 years. - My gosh, that's a great meal.

582
00:26:03,495 --> 00:26:04,724
He wants the kimchi.

583
00:26:04,725 --> 00:26:05,925
No.

584
00:26:07,495 --> 00:26:10,095
It's not that. I'm trying to think of a way to consume it.

585
00:26:10,495 --> 00:26:12,494
But don't we need kimchi while having meat?

586
00:26:12,495 --> 00:26:14,634
That would be a great meal and all.

587
00:26:14,635 --> 00:26:16,334
- But there's a lot of kimchi. - You know what?

588
00:26:16,335 --> 00:26:17,474
I'm having an identity crisis.

589
00:26:17,475 --> 00:26:18,935
- I'm in the Palm Oil Family. - Okay.

590
00:26:19,235 --> 00:26:20,775
- Then I should eat the kimchi. - Yes.

591
00:26:21,445 --> 00:26:22,445
I'm sure it's fermented nicely.

592
00:26:22,446 --> 00:26:23,944
I'm bringing it up for your sake.

593
00:26:23,945 --> 00:26:26,314
You're thinking of it as a keepsake, not food.

594
00:26:26,315 --> 00:26:28,045
Let's just have half of it.

595
00:26:28,315 --> 00:26:29,315
- Really? - It's tasty.

596
00:26:29,316 --> 00:26:31,415
- We'll eat it with your permission. - Let's eat it.

597
00:26:31,615 --> 00:26:33,924
I think my grandma would want us to enjoy it.

598
00:26:33,925 --> 00:26:35,054
- Of course. - Yes.

599
00:26:35,055 --> 00:26:36,094
- That's what she'd want. - Yes.

600
00:26:36,095 --> 00:26:37,724
- I'll serve the bibimbap first. - Thank you.

601
00:26:37,725 --> 00:26:39,964
(As they think of her grandma, the yukhoe bibimbap is served.)

602
00:26:39,965 --> 00:26:41,664
- My gosh. - Here's the sauce.

603
00:26:41,665 --> 00:26:43,094
- The raw beef looks great. - Add it to your food.

604
00:26:43,095 --> 00:26:44,694
- Okay. - The raw beef looks great.

605
00:26:44,695 --> 00:26:46,204
- Gosh, it looks tasty. - Check that out.

606
00:26:46,205 --> 00:26:47,965
How interesting. She added seasoned zucchini.

607
00:26:48,365 --> 00:26:50,575
Gosh, this looks amazing.

608
00:26:50,705 --> 00:26:53,204
There's a butchery around the restaurant.

609
00:26:53,205 --> 00:26:54,404
- It's a famous butchery. - I see.

610
00:26:54,405 --> 00:26:55,504
- That's right. - That's why.

611
00:26:55,505 --> 00:26:56,944
- So... - The beef has a nice colour to it.

612
00:26:56,945 --> 00:26:58,014
You know how it is around cattle markets, right?

613
00:26:58,015 --> 00:26:59,274
- Of course. - Why does it sound familiar?

614
00:26:59,275 --> 00:27:00,285
You seem very disappointed.

615
00:27:01,115 --> 00:27:02,715
- Well... - I'm a good worker too.

616
00:27:03,155 --> 00:27:04,814
- My gosh. - All right. Let's dig in.

617
00:27:04,815 --> 00:27:06,924
- Eat a lot. - Okay.

618
00:27:06,925 --> 00:27:09,625
All right. That way, I can ask you to work hard later.

619
00:27:10,255 --> 00:27:11,925
(Mixing)

620
00:27:15,395 --> 00:27:17,165
You get hungry after crying.

621
00:27:19,805 --> 00:27:21,065
(Humming)

622
00:27:22,105 --> 00:27:23,274
Our energy comes from rice.

623
00:27:23,275 --> 00:27:24,734
That was some high-quality raw beef.

624
00:27:24,735 --> 00:27:26,374
- It was tasty. - It was so good.

625
00:27:26,375 --> 00:27:29,345
- Gosh, the raw beef is amazing. - It's tasty.

626
00:27:29,875 --> 00:27:31,045
(Humming in approval)

627
00:27:33,215 --> 00:27:34,245
(Enjoying his food)

628
00:27:35,585 --> 00:27:36,715
Gosh, the raw beef completes the dish.

629
00:27:37,915 --> 00:27:40,384
From today onward, I'll keep the house clean...

630
00:27:40,385 --> 00:27:42,755
so that my family can come and use it later.

631
00:27:43,125 --> 00:27:44,155
That's a good idea.

632
00:27:44,395 --> 00:27:45,894
When I was born,

633
00:27:45,895 --> 00:27:48,594
my grandma and grandpa built the house themselves.

634
00:27:48,595 --> 00:27:50,395
- When you were born? - Yes.

635
00:27:50,965 --> 00:27:53,334
There is a photo of my grandparents...

636
00:27:53,335 --> 00:27:55,705
stacking up the bricks with me around.

637
00:27:56,035 --> 00:27:57,934
It was taken in December of 1985.

638
00:27:57,935 --> 00:27:59,844
- Your grandma... - Did your grandma build the house?

639
00:27:59,845 --> 00:28:01,244
My grandma and grandpa built it.

640
00:28:01,245 --> 00:28:03,015
- Just the two of them? - They built it with my dad.

641
00:28:03,475 --> 00:28:05,315
- That was why I wanted to clean it. - All right.

642
00:28:06,685 --> 00:28:09,014
Here is your order.

643
00:28:09,015 --> 00:28:10,085
There is pepper.

644
00:28:11,785 --> 00:28:15,284
(Kimchi jjigae and intestine soup will warm up their stomachs.)

645
00:28:15,285 --> 00:28:16,995
- The food is really tasty. - It looks tasty.

646
00:28:17,195 --> 00:28:18,525
It was to die for.

647
00:28:20,525 --> 00:28:21,525
(My goodness)

648
00:28:21,526 --> 00:28:22,864
- My goodness. - This is their signature dish.

649
00:28:22,865 --> 00:28:23,964
Is this their signature dish?

650
00:28:23,965 --> 00:28:26,064
- Yes. - A dish like this is a must here.

651
00:28:26,065 --> 00:28:27,304
The butchery is nearby.

652
00:28:27,305 --> 00:28:28,305
(I agree with you.)

653
00:28:30,505 --> 00:28:31,734
(We can restore our strength and work now!)

654
00:28:31,735 --> 00:28:32,945
This is incredible.

655
00:28:35,305 --> 00:28:36,844
- Didn't you have breakfast? - What?

656
00:28:36,845 --> 00:28:39,074
- Didn't you have breakfast? - This is how much I normally eat.

657
00:28:39,075 --> 00:28:41,184
(Laughing)

658
00:28:41,185 --> 00:28:43,385
Shall we go to the farming machine store first?

659
00:28:43,415 --> 00:28:44,415
- Okay. - Okay.

660
00:28:44,416 --> 00:28:45,985
The farming machine store...

661
00:28:46,285 --> 00:28:48,425
will sell things like gloves and arm sleeves.

662
00:28:49,255 --> 00:28:51,555
- Let's go. - All right.

663
00:28:51,655 --> 00:28:53,225
Thank you for the food.

664
00:28:53,795 --> 00:28:55,024
- It's on me. - What?

665
00:28:55,025 --> 00:28:57,465
Food is on me today.

666
00:28:57,635 --> 00:29:00,535
It was the least I could do since I wasn't paying them.

667
00:29:01,835 --> 00:29:03,535
- Thank you for the food. - Thank you for the food.

668
00:29:04,205 --> 00:29:05,334
Will you go to Seoul right away?

669
00:29:05,335 --> 00:29:06,704
No, we'll clean the house...

670
00:29:06,705 --> 00:29:08,274
- now that we've eaten. - The house.

671
00:29:08,275 --> 00:29:10,244
There's someone who does maintenance work at times,

672
00:29:10,245 --> 00:29:11,674
but it isn't enough since the house is unoccupied.

673
00:29:11,675 --> 00:29:14,085
That's right. That happens...

674
00:29:14,645 --> 00:29:15,985
when the house is unoccupied.

675
00:29:16,585 --> 00:29:17,784
- Thank you. - Thank you.

676
00:29:17,785 --> 00:29:19,085
- Thank you. - We'll come again.

677
00:29:19,985 --> 00:29:22,185
- Shall we go? - Let's go down the street.

678
00:29:24,495 --> 00:29:26,265
What should we do? Shall we buy the tools at a supermarket?

679
00:29:26,895 --> 00:29:29,095
There used to be all the tools in the house.

680
00:29:29,265 --> 00:29:30,664
But now, there was nothing useful.

681
00:29:30,665 --> 00:29:32,095
Everything became rusty and worn.

682
00:29:33,305 --> 00:29:34,534
They're sold here.

683
00:29:34,535 --> 00:29:36,674
(They're sold here.)

684
00:29:36,675 --> 00:29:38,405
We should get three brooms, right?

685
00:29:38,505 --> 00:29:39,804
Aren't they too small?

686
00:29:39,805 --> 00:29:40,845
- But... - Aren't there bigger ones?

687
00:29:41,005 --> 00:29:42,244
- Let's get one of these. - Hello.

688
00:29:42,245 --> 00:29:44,045
- Hello. - Hello.

689
00:29:44,715 --> 00:29:46,485
We need one of these, right?

690
00:29:46,815 --> 00:29:47,915
- What? - For the yard.

691
00:29:49,655 --> 00:29:51,955
Please give me one gridiron pan as well.

692
00:29:52,385 --> 00:29:53,385
- I'll give you one. - Okay.

693
00:29:53,386 --> 00:29:54,824
Do they sell both gridiron pans and brooms?

694
00:29:54,825 --> 00:29:56,054
They sell everything.

695
00:29:56,055 --> 00:29:57,254
- It's a general store. - Hello.

696
00:29:57,255 --> 00:29:59,594
- Hello. - We need two big ones.

697
00:29:59,595 --> 00:30:00,764
- Big ones? - Yes.

698
00:30:00,765 --> 00:30:02,095
That dustpan looks good.

699
00:30:02,525 --> 00:30:04,065
Do you sell work pants?

700
00:30:04,765 --> 00:30:07,135
Hyun Moo, pick a pair of work pants.

701
00:30:08,105 --> 00:30:09,105
Hold on.

702
00:30:09,535 --> 00:30:11,505
- Give me any colour. - I want pink work pants.

703
00:30:13,275 --> 00:30:15,244
- I want this one. - He always buys pink items.

704
00:30:15,245 --> 00:30:16,915
Yes. I'm Moorincess.

705
00:30:19,815 --> 00:30:21,044
A supermarket was right next to the store.

706
00:30:21,045 --> 00:30:22,545
All the places are nearby.

707
00:30:22,955 --> 00:30:25,255
- They have everything. - They sell many items.

708
00:30:26,255 --> 00:30:28,024
Kian84 will pick the right brand of bleach.

709
00:30:28,025 --> 00:30:29,185
He's the bleach rocker.

710
00:30:29,655 --> 00:30:30,854
Bleach.

711
00:30:30,855 --> 00:30:32,855
- He's an expert in bleach. - Bleach rocker.

712
00:30:33,225 --> 00:30:34,894
It'll be nice to have it around.

713
00:30:34,895 --> 00:30:35,924
We bought so many items.

714
00:30:35,925 --> 00:30:37,994
You'll use them when you organise the house.

715
00:30:37,995 --> 00:30:38,995
Of course.

716
00:30:40,805 --> 00:30:42,235
We had to drink coffee.

717
00:30:42,665 --> 00:30:43,905
Coffee mix packets are the best.

718
00:30:44,475 --> 00:30:45,535
All right.

719
00:30:45,705 --> 00:30:47,745
We bought the items quickly to get back to work.

720
00:30:49,475 --> 00:30:50,645
Hyun Moo, it's heavy.

721
00:30:51,415 --> 00:30:53,345
It's okay. You can carry that.

722
00:30:53,585 --> 00:30:55,145
- Give me that. - Here.

723
00:30:55,485 --> 00:30:56,655
Right.

724
00:30:56,985 --> 00:30:58,084
- I feel like I'm dying. - Thank you.

725
00:30:58,085 --> 00:30:59,284
- Thank you. - Thank you.

726
00:30:59,285 --> 00:31:00,325
Take care.

727
00:31:01,255 --> 00:31:02,285
My goodness.

728
00:31:03,095 --> 00:31:04,495
- Oh, no. I feel bad. - It's okay.

729
00:31:07,265 --> 00:31:08,794
When did he open an ice cream packet?

730
00:31:08,795 --> 00:31:10,195
When did he get ice cream?

731
00:31:11,095 --> 00:31:12,165
Are you okay?

732
00:31:12,295 --> 00:31:13,734
We bought so many liquid items.

733
00:31:13,735 --> 00:31:15,934
Your back is very bent.

734
00:31:15,935 --> 00:31:18,005
- I felt so bad. - You just need to walk fast.

735
00:31:20,075 --> 00:31:21,645
It's raining too.

736
00:31:24,575 --> 00:31:25,945
Kian84 became speechless due to exhaustion.

737
00:31:27,285 --> 00:31:28,315
Are you okay?

738
00:31:28,885 --> 00:31:29,955
It's too heavy, right?

739
00:31:30,285 --> 00:31:32,215
- Let's hurry up and go. - Let's hurry up and go.

740
00:31:32,685 --> 00:31:33,724
(He hugs the wet box.)

741
00:31:33,725 --> 00:31:35,855
The bottom will tear if he doesn't hold it like that.

742
00:31:36,025 --> 00:31:37,995
(Heave-ho)

743
00:31:39,255 --> 00:31:40,324
For goodness' sake.

744
00:31:40,325 --> 00:31:42,195
(Dropping)

745
00:31:44,635 --> 00:31:45,695
We're nearly there.

746
00:31:46,835 --> 00:31:47,934
Throw it.

747
00:31:47,935 --> 00:31:49,035
(Groaning)

748
00:31:49,265 --> 00:31:50,435
Well done.

749
00:31:52,775 --> 00:31:54,344
(He becomes one with the wet box.)

750
00:31:54,345 --> 00:31:55,405
Well done.

751
00:31:55,945 --> 00:31:57,974
- My goodness. - It must weigh over 20kg.

752
00:31:57,975 --> 00:31:59,015
Well done.

753
00:31:59,075 --> 00:32:00,385
- Let's hurry up and change. - Okay.

754
00:32:00,945 --> 00:32:02,885
- Take a pair of work pants each. - Work pants.

755
00:32:03,085 --> 00:32:04,315
- Where are the work pants? - Here.

756
00:32:05,285 --> 00:32:06,525
Whose pants are these?

757
00:32:07,385 --> 00:32:09,285
- Na Rae, these are yours. - Yes, give me those.

758
00:32:09,525 --> 00:32:11,095
Na Rae's pants have the original colours.

759
00:32:11,325 --> 00:32:12,924
The pink pants are mine.

760
00:32:12,925 --> 00:32:15,195
- He likes bright colours. - The Indian pants are yours.

761
00:32:15,995 --> 00:32:17,664
It'll be okay if it doesn't rain harder.

762
00:32:17,665 --> 00:32:19,495
It'll be perfect. Then there won't be sunlight.

763
00:32:20,505 --> 00:32:21,964
Your grandma is helping us.

764
00:32:21,965 --> 00:32:24,074
- So that you wouldn't feel hot? - This weather is much better.

765
00:32:24,075 --> 00:32:26,305
- This is better. - Yes. It was so hot earlier.

766
00:32:26,645 --> 00:32:28,275
I'll go and change.

767
00:32:30,445 --> 00:32:32,945
(Turning around)

768
00:32:34,645 --> 00:32:35,944
(Taking off his pants)

769
00:32:35,945 --> 00:32:36,985
Let's pluck them out.

770
00:32:38,815 --> 00:32:39,884
(Moorincess' transformation)

771
00:32:39,885 --> 00:32:42,585
- My goodness. - My goodness.

772
00:32:42,855 --> 00:32:43,855
My goodness.

773
00:32:44,155 --> 00:32:46,665
(He feels refreshed.)

774
00:32:47,095 --> 00:32:48,764
